## Does it read as a lily pad at 128 px, and does the frog fit?

- Sprites (128 px, elevation 30, 8 directions): YES. At 1x on a pond blue backdrop all 8 read as a green dish with a V notch and faint radial veins.
  The sprite is 80 to 82 px wide and 45 to 46 px high (sprites/metrics.json).
- 3D renders (out/lily-pad/render.png, the card): YES. A round pale mint dish, a dark green wall, a crisp V.
- Cutouts (front, three-quarter): NO. Both have the same box, cols 307..716 and rows 974..1007 (410 x 34 px). Each is an edge-on green slab.
  At the 128 px scale (1/8) the pad would be about 51 x 4 px. The cause is the tool: `./forge cutout` sets elevation 0 for every view unless
  `--el` is given (src/cli/forge.ts:383). The maker log names the front cutout only. The three-quarter cutout is also a sliver (N1).
- Frog fit: YES, with no spare room (N2). The feet footprint of the frog is 0.347 x 0.166 m. Its smallest enclosing circle has radius 0.1736 m.
  The pad radius is 0.200 m, so the leaf margin is 26 mm at the haunch feet. The frog is 0.346 m tall and 87 percent of the pad width.

