The maker disclosed all four in the log, and that no frog-on-pad render exists. I made no such render either. I measured the fit on the GLB files instead.

## What the song scene (W6 line 9, "I can see a frog. Hop, hop!", set "lily pad", props "frog, lily pad") needs

Book row: "lily pad | 6 | 1 (1) | frog hops from it" (monorepo forge-inventory.md section 5). The row gives no size and no colour.

1. The route decides. A 3D stage (src/song) loads the GLB as a prop, so the pad works as built. A 2D compositor needs a look-down cutout.
   Order one cutout at about `--el 35` in a separate folder (one folder keeps one ppm, canvas, and foot point). The near rim falls about 117 px below the foot row,
   so the margin must be about 135 px or more. I did not run this (N1).
2. The pad and the frog need a size change in the stage. The pad scaled 1.3 to 1.5 gives 86 to 126 mm of leaf around the feet. The frog at about 0.7 gives about 78 mm (N2).
3. The frog stands on the pad top at y about 0.018 and about 0.03 m back of the centre. The centred frog overhangs the V by up to 9 mm at the inner front feet (N2).
4. The camera for the shot needs an elevation of 30 degrees or more. The stage example key uses el 12, which shows the pad as an ellipse 0.083 m high (N2).
5. The pond asset has its own pads in a yellow green (#7cc23c, #5a9a2a). This pad is blue green (#5fa364, #4f8f5a). Align them if both show (N2).
6. The frog has no hop clip (idle, walk, attack, hit, death). The hop is stage work or a new clip, outside this step (N2).

## Rating

Criteria scores (1 to 5): brief match 4, silhouette 3.5, proportion and appeal 3.5, shape language 3.5, value and colour 3, materials 3.5,
detail hierarchy 3, technical quality 4, game readiness 3, readability at 128 px 4. The sum is 35.0. The mean is 3.5, and that gives 7.0 of 10.

- Brief match (4): every measured value agrees with the brief: 0.400 m wide, top at 0.0319 m, dish 0.004 m, notch 30 degrees, 9 veins of 0.006 m, 3812 triangles.
  The veins start 15 mm from the centre and not at the centre.
- Technical quality (4): mech-check ok, 3812 triangles, bottomY 0, no warning, typecheck 0, a deterministic build.
- Value and colour (3) and detail hierarchy (3): the veins are faint (N3), and the notch cut face reads as a blocky step in the cutout.
- Game readiness (3): the cutouts cannot serve a 2D pond scene, and the frog fills the pad (N1, N2).
- Readability at 128 px (4): the sprites read clearly. The cutouts do not, and this keeps the score at 4.
- A drop of 0.5 in any one criterion gives a mean of 6.9, so the result is at the bar and not above it.

## Findings (all nonblocking)

- N1 [Medium] The 2 delivered cutouts are the same edge-on slab (410 x 34 px). The tool sets elevation 0 for every view. They show no veins and no dish.
  The route decides if this matters (see above). Suggested change: one look-down cutout in a separate folder. | owner: orchestrator, then maker
- N2 [Medium] The frog fits with 26 mm of leaf, and it fills 87 percent of the pad width. The scene needs a bigger pad or a smaller frog, a placement, a higher camera,
  a colour match, and a hop. See the list above. | owner: orchestrator
- N3 [Low] The veins are faint: 7.2 percent luminance difference, about 1.2 px at 128 px. They do not carry the read. The PM chose the colours. Optional: a darker vein or 0.010 m width.
- N4 [Low] The brief says the frog is 0.347 m x 0.222 m "at the feet" and that the feet "touch the rim at the notch". Measured: 0.222 m is the body depth with the head. The feet depth is 0.166 m.
  The front toes near the V stand about 0.09 m from the centre, not at the rim. Suggested change: correct the text. | owner: maker
- N5 [Nit] Sharp notch edges, a thick rolled rim, and a ten-fold vein fan with 1 vein cut by the notch (the notch sits 6 degrees off the centre of the 72 degree gap). All are within the brief. No change needed now.
- N6 [Info] Commit scope is clean. f8e89036 adds the 2 acceptance-splash files, and its title names them. The working tree holds other modified files that no commit in the range contains.
- N7 [Info] docs/storytime-song.md:80-83 does not name the lily pad and still says "Not built: duck, kite, ball, grape, sun, cloud, easel". The doc owner updates it after the look check.

